  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Gilded Grove",
    "overview": "The site reads as a clearing at golden hour. Amber is the light that falls through the canopy; cream parchment is the page it lands on; oxblood is the ink. Everything else is paper, bark, and leaf. The system is warm before it is modern, and hand-bound before it is systematic. There is one page material and two inks: light mode is a single sheet of pale cream paper lit from above, one soft amber light entering at the top edge, dark mode is the same room after sunset with the same light from above. Body copy is ink on paper in both modes; amber never becomes text colour, because amber here is light, and light does not carry meaning. The system runs two registers. The default register is the garden: calm, reading-first, one column, with craft concentrated in the ruled h2, the SVG page divider and the bark-plaque code block. The second register is the tabletop handbook, activated only under the D&D route classes.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Amber primary with a seven-step ramp; oxblood heading ink in light mode, amber heading ink in dark mode.",
      "Warm, low-opacity shadows tinted amber (never neutral grey) on paper surfaces.",
      "Irregular compound corner radii for anything that reads as a cut sheet or a plaque.",
      "Reading-first density: 16px body at 1.625 line height, 280px sidebar, one content column.",
      "Craft artifacts over ornament: SVG divider, ruled h2, leaf-lit code plaque.",
      "Handbook sub-theme that is explicitly scoped to a route and never leaks."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Two Inks Rule",
        "body": "Amber is light; ink is text. Body copy is never amber and never a link colour. If a passage needs emphasis, it gets weight or oxblood, not the accent.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Canopy Light Rule",
        "body": "Amber enters the page exactly once, as one soft radial at the top edge that has faded out before the first screen ends. No surface carries its own gradient; the light belongs to the page and falls over every surface on it.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Accent Rule",
        "body": "Amber is the only interactive hue. Oxblood, the leaf trio, and the ledger greys never become hover or focus colours. Adding a fourth accent hue breaks the world.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Status-Only Green Rule",
        "body": "Green appears in this system only as a freshness signal, always as a 12% tint behind a dark-shade label. It never becomes a bullet, a highlight, an illustration fill, or a success message elsewhere.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The 16/26 Rule",
        "body": "Body copy is 16px on a 26px line (1.625). A 110% base was tried and replaced; do not reintroduce it. Long-form reading quality is the site's most load-bearing visual decision. Note the mechanism: `--ifm-font-size-base` is declared twice, as `110%` in `custom.css` and as `16px` in `custom-narrow-styles.css`, and the second wins only because that file is imported last. The same applies to the system UI stack, which shadows an unused `\"Open Sans\"` declaration a few lines earlier. The computed value is the only one that counts; the earlier declarations are dead weight, not a second opinion.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Handbook Quarantine Rule",
        "body": "BookInstanity, MrEavesRemake, ScalySans, the drop cap and the small-caps first line apply only inside `html[class*=\"-doc-id-DnD/\"]`. They never appear on a dashboard, a landing page, or a general article.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two-Weight Rule",
        "body": "Reading text uses 400, emphasis 450 to 700, and mono never exceeds 450. Weight is the system's emphasis tool; colour is not.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Warm Shadow Rule",
        "body": "If a shadow falls on paper, it is `rgba(163, 106, 0, ...)`. Black shadows are an exception for the handbook container and dark-mode hovers, not a default.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Settle Rule",
        "body": "Hover does not scale, bounce or glow. It changes the shadow from rest to lifted over 0.2s ease-in-out. Motion in this system is a sheet being picked up, nothing faster.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "keep body copy at 16px on a 26px line (1.625), and keep paragraph margins tight (0.5em bottom).",
      "give every h2 the full-width 2px gold rule, and give h3 nothing.",
      "use the compound radius `28px 12px 35px 15px` for anything that reads as a cut sheet: code blocks, admonitions, terminal frames.",
      "tint paper shadows amber (`rgba(163, 106, 0, .4)` at rest, `.7` on hover) and animate them over 0.2s ease-in-out.",
      "reach for `--ifm-color-primary` and its seven-step family instead of writing new amber hex values.",
      "use the SVG divider on `hr`, and the leaf trio on full-width terminal frames only.",
      "scope handbook typography and the parchment texture to the `-doc-id-DnD/` route classes, and give those components their own `--dnd-*` tokens.",
      "route every focus indicator through `--focus-ring` (`#8f5d00` light, `#ffb630` dark). Amber at #e99700 is 2.26:1 on paper and is never a focus colour.",
      "keep green, stale-amber and outdated-red inside the freshness family, always as a 12% tint with a dark-shade label, never as a bare fill.",
      "prefer a 9999px pill or a 3px hairline to a mid-range radius; the system has no 12px-to-24px middle ground."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "set body copy in amber, and don't make amber a heading colour in light mode. Headings are oxblood there.",
      "put the warm gradient anywhere except the first and last 1% of the viewport edges.",
      "introduce a fourth accent hue. Amber, oxblood and the decorative leaf trio are the whole palette.",
      "use neutral grey shadows on paper surfaces; the dark-mode card hover (`#AAA3`) and the handbook container are the only exceptions.",
      "reuse the handbook's red rule (#9c2b1b) as an error colour, or the leaf red as a danger state.",
      "ship white-on-amber text. `#fff` on #e99700 is 2.36:1. Amber fills carry ink (`--ink`, 6.77:1) or use amber-darkest as the fill with white text (4.55:1).",
      "apply the organic radius, the leaf trio or the drop cap outside their artifacts. They are signatures, and repeating them everywhere spends them.",
      "set Roboto outside table cells and the table of contents; prose is the system UI stack.",
      "animate anything on scroll except the 0.1-speed hero parallax.",
      "put a hardcoded type size in a component CSS module when an Infima variable already carries it; the two-register type system depends on those variables being the single source."
    ]
  }
}
